  "description": "Governed Jira Cloud automation for RailCall — seventeen commands covering the full issue lifecycle plus multi-step composites, over the Jira REST API v3 (Basic Auth with an Atlassian API token stored in the RailCall vault; egress allowlisted to *.atlassian.net and *.jira.com).\n\nWHO IT'S FOR\nEngineering teams who want an AI agent to run day-to-day Jira hygiene — triage, follow-ups, status moves, assignment, attachments — without raw credentials or unreviewed writes. Every mutating command is dry-run-first: RailCall previews the exact payload and requires explicit approval; each approved run yields a signed receipt.\n\nREAD (low risk)\n- getIssue — one issue by key/id (summary, status, assignee, fields).\n- searchIssues — JQL via POST /search/jql (legacy GET /search removed 2025); token pagination, no total.\n- listIssueTypes — instance-wide types.\n- getTransitions — valid transitions + ids for an issue (feed these to transitionIssue).\n- listProjects — accessible projects.\n- getProjectIssueTypes — valid types for one project (createmeta).\n\nWRITE (medium risk, approval-gated)\n- createIssue — create; plain text auto-converted to ADF.\n- updateIssue — edit summary/description.\n- addComment — comment (ADF).\n- transitionIssue — move by transition id.\n- assignUser — by accountId or email (resolved via /user/search).\n- attachFile — upload text/base64 (X-Atlassian-Token: no-check).\n\nCOMPOSITES (several API calls under ONE approval)\n- triageIssue — fetch issue, post triage comment, optionally transition.\n- resolveWithNote — closing note + transition together.\n- cloneIssue — copy an issue into a new one (summary suffix, description, type).\n- bulkTransitionFromJql — transition every issue matching a JQL (cap 200); per-issue outcomes reported, never retried.\n\nDESTRUCTIVE (high risk, approval-gated)\n- deleteIssue — delete, optionally subtasks.\n\nQUICK START\n1. Token: id.atlassian.com → Security → API tokens.\n2. Studio → Integrations: entry \"edudzi-jira\" (or \"jira\") with JIRA_DOMAIN, JIRA_EMAIL, JIRA_API_TOKEN — vault-only, never env vars.\n3. railcall market install edudzi-jira && railcall studio.\n4. jira.listProjects → jira.getProjectIssueTypes → jira.createIssue {project_key, summary, issue_type}; discover ids via jira.getTransitions, then jira.transitionIssue.\n\nERROR BEHAVIOR\nHTTP >= 400 raises loudly, never returned as data; field errors surfaced verbatim (e.g. issuetype: Specify a valid issue type). Writes never auto-retry — a flaky network cannot create duplicates. Bulk reports per-item outcomes explicitly. Issue types are project-specific (Product Discovery accepts only \"Idea\").\n\ncontest:2026Q3",
